# Cookies from up to three logged-in burner X sessions, used round-robin so
# the app can sustain ~3 req/sec (1 req/sec per burner) instead of one
# account's worth of rate limit.
#
# For each burner: log in at x.com in a browser, then:
#   DevTools (F12) -> Application -> Storage -> Cookies -> https://x.com
# and copy these two values.
#
# Cookies rather than a password on purpose: X's scripted login flow triggers
# email/phone challenges and is the fastest way to get a burner locked.
# They last weeks - re-paste when you start seeing auth errors.
#
# Only X_AUTH_TOKEN_1/X_CT0_1 is required; add _2 and _3 to grow the pool.
# A lone unindexed X_AUTH_TOKEN/X_CT0 pair also still works as a single burner.
X_AUTH_TOKEN_1=
X_CT0_1=
X_AUTH_TOKEN_2=
X_CT0_2=
X_AUTH_TOKEN_3=
X_CT0_3=

# Optional: path to the Python running the fetcher (defaults to "python")
PYTHON_BIN=python
